A struct the target requires, copied from a struct the source has as
optional, where the struct requires a field of its own: an instance that
lacks the struct has nothing to fill it with, so the lens is not total, and
bind refuses it. 1.0 requires q beneath o, and q requires a, which 0.0 has
only where it has o.q. The remedy is _coalesce with a struct fallback
(coalesce-struct).
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		q?: {
			a!: int
			z?: int
		}
	}
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		q: {
			a!: int
		}
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		o: {
			q: {
				z: _drop
			}
		}
	}
}
-- out/bind --
error[E0382]: o.q.a in the ForwardLens in 1.0.thema is not total for some instance
 --> 1.0.thema:9:1
  |
9 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: o.q.a in the ForwardLens in 1.0.thema is required by 1.0.thema, and is written only under v0_0.o.q.a != _|_, which the checker cannot show cover every instance under v0_0.o != _|_; write it unconditionally, under a condition and its negation, or under type tests covering every alternative of the tested field
  = note: a lens must be total: every instance of the schema in history/0.0.thema must translate to an instance of the schema in 1.0.thema (totality rule unknown-exhaustive)
  = help: write the mapping in a form the checker can follow, or add a lacuna where it cannot decide
-- out/decompiled/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		q: {
			a!: int
		}
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		o: {
			q: {
				z: _drop
			}
		}
	}
}
-- out/decompiled/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		q?: {
			a!: int
			z?: int
		}
	}
}
-- out/normal.cue --
name: "ship"
schemas: {
	"0": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				o?: {
					q?: {
						a!: int
						z?: int
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
	"1": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				o?: {
					q: {
						a!: int
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
lenses: {
	"0.0->1.0": {
		v0_0: _
		v1_0: {if v0_0.o != _|_ {
			o:
				q: {if v0_0.o.q.a != _|_ {
					a: v0_0.o.q.a
				}}
		}}
		lacunas: [{
			@thema(derived)
			condition: v0_0.o.q.z != _|_
			sourceFields: [{
				path:  "o.q.z"
				value: v0_0.o.q.z
			}]
			message: "o.q.z has no equivalent in 1.0 and was dropped"
			type:    "DroppedField"
		}]
	}
	"1.0->0.0": {
		v1_0: _
		v0_0: {if v1_0.o != _|_ {
			o: v1_0.o
		}}
	}
}
